Key Takeaways
•	Preventive controls stop or reduce the chance of an attack.
•	Detective controls identify attacks, anomalies, or incidents.
•	Corrective controls contain, fix, and recover from incidents.
•	Compensating controls provide an alternative risk-reduction measure when the primary control is not feasible.
